      "content": "Biometric sensors in standard office furniture do not currently exist at a level sensitive enough to read heart rate or facial micro-expressions through the upholstery in real-time while an employee sits there. Even the most advanced research-level prototypes require specialized equipment and cannot be concealed inside heavy-duty foam padding for daily office use. There is no method of \"masking\" your vitals with clothing or posture because the technology simply isn't capable of detecting such signals through solid materials or fabric layers in the way you describe. To resolve this, your best course of action is to verify the chair's warranty and documentation directly from the manufacturer or your IT security team, regardless of the source of authorization.",
